<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hanau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-sixth-coalition">War of the Sixth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hanau was fought on 30–31 October 1813 near Hanau in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, where an Austro-Bavarian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-philipp-von-wrede">Karl Philipp von Wrede</a> tried to cut off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s retreat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after his defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>. Napoleon broke through and reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> had changed sides only weeks earlier under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ried">Treaty of Ried</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hanau.jpg" alt="Battle of Hanau" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vernet-Battle_of_Hanau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
